    "body": "<!-- relay-run-log -->\n**Relay run log** — issue #240\n\n- 2026-09-11 11:32Z — Relay picked up this issue for a BB worker run.\n- 2026-09-11 12:12Z — Relay BB run pushed an update. Pull request: #379 Tokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000 Pushed branch `bb/relay-240-generic-rest-04-09-expose-database-and-thr_du897t2mt8` to origin. ## Summary Implements issue #240: exposes database and property metadata operations over the generic REST layer. - `GET/POST /api/databases`, `GET/PATCH/DELETE /api/databases/:id` — `DELETE` archives rather than hard-deleting; a `system: true` database returns 403 (`forbidden`) on archive. - `POST /api/databases/:id/properties`, `PATCH/DELETE /api/properties/:id` — enforce `schema_locked` (database) and `locked` (property) as 403 with matching error codes; `schema_locked`/`property_locked` are now their own error classes (still 403, per the #238 contract) instead of a generic `ForbiddenError`. - Changing a property's `type` via `PATCH` returns 202 after enqueueing the existing `migration_status` job (#21) — the endpoint never migrates inline. - All routes are thin mappings onto `createChokePoint`'s service calls, resolve display names/labels through the #35 localized-metadata catalog, authenticate via the existing adapter, and never return 204 on a successful mutation. - Extracted a shared `routeTable.ts` (`RouteDefinition`/`mountRoutes`) so these new generic resource routes and the #239 module custom routes share one path-compiling/dispatch implementation instead of duplicating it. New tests: `databasesHandler.test.ts` (7 tests) and `propertiesHandler.test.ts` (9 tests) cover CRUD/archive/lock/type-migration paths, including the forbidden system-database archive, `schema_locked`/`property_locked` 403s, the 202-plus-exactly-one-enqueued-job assertion for a type change, and that no successful mutation returns 204. `routeMatrix.ts`/`chokePointWriteBoundary.unit.test.ts` were extended to cover the 8 new routes end-to-end (auth-required, choke-point-only writes). Verified: `backend`'s full `pnpm run verify` (lint, format, build, unit/integration/e2e tests — 961 + 5 tests) and `web`'s full `pnpm run verify` (lint, format, build, 139 tests) both pass with no regressions. Relay-Step-Status: pass\n- 2026-09-11 12:42Z — Relay BB run pushed an update. Pull request: #379 Tokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000 Pushed to branch `bb/relay-240-generic-rest-04-09-expose-database-and-thr_du897t2mt8` (updates existing PR #379, no new branch or PR created). This push addresses the three code-review findings from PR #379's CI run: 1. **High (correctness)** — `PATCH /api/properties/:id` applied name/config/type changes as three separate transactions, so a 403 from a locked config/type change could leave an already-committed rename behind. Fixed with a new `chokePoint.updateProperty` that applies all requested fields in one transaction, rolling back everything if any part is rejected. 2. **Medium (correctness)** — `GET /api/databases` built a fresh `CatalogResolver` per database in the list. Fixed to build one resolver per request and reuse it. 3. **Medium (test-coverage)** — `renameDatabase`/`listDatabases` had only HTTP-layer coverage. Added choke-point-level unit tests for both, plus for the new `updateProperty` (including its rollback-on-rejection behavior). Full `pnpm run verify` passes in both `backend` (lint, format, build, 966 integration tests, 5 e2e tests) and `web` (lint, format, build, 139 tests), with no regressions. Relay-Step-Status: pass\n- 2026-09-11 13:13Z — Relay BB run pushed an update. Pull request: #379 Tokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000 Branch `bb/relay-240-generic-rest-04-09-expose-database-and-thr_du897t2mt8` is pushed and up to date on origin, with all work through commit `7d985c1` (the latest review-fix, adding choke-point test coverage for `updateProperty`'s config branch including the rollup backfill path). Relay-Step-Status: pass\n- 2026-09-11 13:37Z — Relay BB run pushed an update. Pull request: #379 Tokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000 Pushed to branch `bb/relay-240-generic-rest-04-09-expose-database-and-thr_du897t2mt8` (commit `e423a1d`). This push addresses the latest review round on PR #379: - **2 HIGH findings fixed**: `POST /api/databases/:id/properties` and `PATCH /api/properties/:id` now validate the request's `type` string against `PROPERTY_TYPES` at the handler boundary, throwing a 400 `validation_failed` before the previously-unchecked `as PropertyType` cast, instead of relying solely on the downstream store check. - **1 low-severity suggestion fixed**: `POST /api/databases/:id/properties` now fetches the target database before creating the property, so a database that disappears mid-request can't 404 a mutation that already committed. - **AC gap fixed**: added a `DELETE /api/properties/:id` test against a schema-locked database, plus new 400 tests for an unknown property type on both routes. - **AC gap not implemented (reasoned disagreement)**: the review's AC table claims `PATCH /api/databases/:id` must 403 for `system: true` databases, but issue #240's own Task text scopes that 403 to \"archive and delete\" only, not rename — and the existing rename-is-always-allowed behavior mirrors `renameProperty`'s established convention and is already covered by a passing test. Left as-is. `pnpm run verify` passes cleanly in both `backend/` (204 unit + 971 integration + 5 e2e tests) and `web/` (139 tests). Relay-Step-Status: pass\n- 2026-09-11 13:50Z — This issue was resolved by #379, which just merged into develop.",
